# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# DotEnvLoader reads repo-root `.env` on startup, so the Nuke ingest targets
# pick these up transparently. An env var already set in your shell WINS over
# anything here — which is how you point one run somewhere else without editing
# the file.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL — the default, and deliberately so
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave TAMP_FINDINGS_URL UNSET. Build.cs then defaults to
# http://localhost:5080, so an ingest target run by accident writes to the
# instance on your own machine rather than to a shared one.
#
# The safe target should be the one you get without thinking about it.

# Mint against your LOCAL instance: Settings > Ingest tokens.
#
# A token is per-instance. A token minted on the cluster will not authenticate
# against localhost — it just 401s — so these are not interchangeable and you
# want one of each.
TAMP_FINDINGS_INGEST_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLUSTER — uncomment BOTH only for a deliberate roll to prod
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Uncomment as a PAIR, and comment them back out afterwards.
#
# The URL without the matching token gives a confusing 401. The token without
# the URL silently aims prod credentials at localhost. Neither half is useful
# on its own.
#
# The build prints a banner whenever it is posting anywhere that is not
# localhost, so a forgotten uncomment is visible rather than silent.

# TAMP_FINDINGS_URL=https://tamp-findings.example
# TAMP_FINDINGS_INGEST_TOKEN=cli_...
